# DIAGNOSTICS

`<file>:<line>: <problem>` for a mutants file that isn't one; `the unchanged <suite> fails`; `its find isn't in <path>`; `its find occurs <n> times in <path>, not once`; `the edit doesn't build`.

# BUGS

It isn't part of `vx ci`: a change to a suite or to what its mutants edit prints, under `vx test --changed`, that `vx mutate` is at risk, and it is run by name.
Only SwiftPM test targets can be suites.
A copy's first build takes as long as the target's own.
The measure lines are compared as they print, so a line with a time in it never matches the control's.
The edits are text: an edit that makes the code not build is an error, not a catch.
